    "item": {
     "type": "agentMessage",
     "id": "da54ac74d5-i8",
     "text": "**No, not manually, and with an important distinction between plugins:**\n\n1. **`workflows` (built-in) vs. `workflow` (standalone):**\n   * Playbooks depend on BB's built-in **`workflows`** engine (`id: \"workflows\"`), **not** the separate third-party/standalone **`workflow`** plugin (which uses `.workflow/` scripts).\n\n2. **Automatic enablement:**\n   * You do **not** need to manually enable the `workflows` plugin beforehand.\n   * Playbooks includes an `autoEnableWorkflows` setting (enabled by default in [server.ts](file:///Users/dev/Documents/bb-plugin-playbooks/server.ts#L266-L270)).\n   * When a playbook runs, [`ensureWorkflows()`](file:///Users/dev/Documents/bb-plugin-playbooks/server.ts#L469-L477) automatically verifies whether `workflows` is active and enables it on your behalf via `bb.sdk.plugins.enable({ pluginId: \"workflows\" })` if it was disabled.\n\nThe only scenario where manual intervention is required is if you explicitly disabled the `autoEnableWorkflows` setting in Playbooks' settings (`autoEnableWorkflows: false`)."
    }
   }
  },
